  "text": "Wealthy women funded the entire ministry. Luke chapter eight, and it is three verses that get skipped constantly. Jesus is going throughout every city and village preaching, and the twelve are with him. And then Luke says, and certain women, which had been healed of evil spirits and infirmities. He names them. Mary called Magdalene, out of whom went seven devils. And Joanna the wife of Chuza, Herod's steward. Stop on that one. Herod's steward. That is a household manager inside the royal court, which means Joanna had access and money and a great deal to lose. And Susanna. And many others. And then the line. Which ministered unto him of their substance. Their substance. Their own resources. The most famous ministry in history was underwritten by a group of women, one of them connected to the court of the king who had John the Baptist killed. Luke names them on purpose. He did not have to. He wanted somebody three thousand years later to know exactly who paid for it.",
